- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/convolve3.html
- Summary (EN): The Convolve 3x3 node applies a 3x3 convolution kernel to a layer, computing each output pixel from its 3x3 neighbourhood. It is commonly used for sharpening (default), edge detection and neighbourhood counting. Available since version 20.5.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Convolve 3x3 applique un noyau 3x3 à chaque pixel, à partir de son voisinage immédiat, pour la netteté, la détection de contours ou le comptage de voisinage.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: the layer to convolve", "mask (optional): per-pixel mask amount scaled by the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type accepted by source", "Mask: default 1, only the new value is used", "Toggle RGB, Red, Green, Blue, Alpha: channels affected", "Multiplicative (Top, Middle, Bottom): 3x3 grid of coefficients on the neighbourhood", "Multiplicative Uniform Scale: scales all coefficients", "Normalize Kernel: divides by the coefficient sum so brightness is kept", "Additive (Top, Middle, Bottom): values added to neighbourhood pixels, default 0", "Additive Uniform Scale", "Combine Operation: Add, Multiply, Maximum, Minimum", "Active Terms: which neighbourhood pixels contribute; turning terms off improves performance but limits kernel shape", "Clamp Below Zero / Clamp Above One", "Treat RGBA as Premultiplied: un-premultiplies before the kernel and re-premultiplies after; turn off when blurring colour and alpha together"]

- Caveats: ["Convolution happens in buffer space, so it does not respect pixel scale", "Normalize Kernel has no effect when the kernel sums to zero (e.g. the Outline recipe)", "Edge detection on premultiplied RGB reports edges where opacity varies", "Turning off Active Terms restricts the kernel to specific shapes"]

